1
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:34,040
The only thing I can do
is I can't wait for it.

2
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:38,400
I can't wait for it.

3
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,420
What can I do in the sky?

4
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:51,920
But I don't know what I'm expecting.

5
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:19,660
Oh, my love.

6
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:38,237
Leomon and OgreMon
decided to stop fighting

7
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:40,597
each other and face Metal Etemon together.

8
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:43,997
Meanwhile, the rest of the gang had
their own problems with PuppetMon,

9
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:47,277
but thanks to a brief appearance
by Matt and Metal Garurumon,

10
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,077
he finally got his strings cut,

11
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,160
risking all to Say, me, me, Saber,

12
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:54,097
Liamond threw himself in
front of a vicious blast.

13
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,357
I did you vault to Zudomon
and used my Vulcan's

14
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:59,057
hammer to put a serious dent
in Metal Edomon's armor.

15
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:01,357
We thought Liamond would
return to a Digi-Egg,

16
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,457
but Primary Village was poisoned by evil,

17
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:07,481
and it'll stay that way until all
of the Dark Masters are defeated.

18
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:17,960
This road has to be
going somewhere, right?

19
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,660
Don't count on it.

20
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:24,996
Nothing is certain in the digi-world.

21
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:30,000
Do you have a furball, Kari?

22
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,620
No, silly. I'm okay.

23
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:36,313
One thing is certain only a
cactus could love this place.

24
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:40,370
Kari!

25
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,417
She has to stay out of the sun,

26
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,735
and we've got to find a way
to get her fever down soon.

27
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:50,970
Don't worry.

28
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,179
I won't leave you.

29
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:54,490
Yeah.

30
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:57,377
How come you didn't say
something before now, Kari?

31
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,557
If we'd known sooner, we could
have rested until you felt better.

32
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,470
You mad?

33
00:03:01,553 --> 00:03:03,618
I didn't want to slow everyone down.

34
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:06,920
Oh, I'm not mad.

35
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,840
I wasn't paying attention.

36
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:18,317
We probably shouldn't have
even brought her along.

37
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,230
Huh?

38
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:20,577
What are you talking about?

39
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,577
We had to bring her.

40
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,897
We need her if we want
to save the Digi-world.

41
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:25,277
She's one of the Digidestined.

42
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,517
Have you forgotten that?

43
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:30,437
Not at all, but her being sick, we
should have left her someplace safe.

44
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:33,657
We should have split up so someone could
take care of her while the others looked.

45
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:34,570
Split up?

46
00:03:34,653 --> 00:03:35,757
Tai, this isn't like you.

47
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,180
I'm just a little worried about her.

48
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,735
It's all a part of what I do
to be a good leader, Izzy.

49
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,137
Uh, yeah, but...

50
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:44,640
Izzy, I found it!

51
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:46,610
Huh?

52
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:47,523
We're saved!

53
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,820
Look right up ahead.

54
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,800
You wanted civilization?

55
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,160
Well, it doesn't get
more civilized than this.

56
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,160
Is that America?

57
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,630
Huh?

58
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,437
Well, that's New York City.

59
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,840
But that isn't. That's Rome.

60
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,917
We studied it in geography, and up there,
that's the Arc de Triomphe in Paris.

61
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,765
They're all smooshed together.

62
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,720
It's like that theme park in Florida.

63
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:18,079
Except that this place is deserted.

64
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,871
Look, there's not a sign of life anywhere.

65
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,880
Hey, Izzy, Kari's getting worse.

66
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:26,357
Let's find some place to land.

67
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,381
Oh, yeah, right.

68
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,774
Uh, this looks like a nice, quiet spot.

69
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,877
These cupboards are empty.

70
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,901
There's not even a speck of food.

71
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:40,680
Hey, this what you're looking for?

72
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,600
All right, way to go.

73
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,797
What is it, Agumon?

74
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:45,117
Did you find some aspirin?

75
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,141
Yeah, this ought to do the trick.

76
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,340
It's empty!

77
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,480
Just like everything
else, this place is weird.

78
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:55,860
Tai, humans aren't supposed to
be this color, are they? Mm-mm.

79
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:57,990
Well?

80
00:04:58,073 --> 00:05:01,197
I'm afraid to leave in case something
happens, but she needs medicine.

81
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,574
She's stable, I think.

82
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:05,437
All we can do now is hope
her fever breaks soon.

83
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,350
It will.

84
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:09,137
Least I know I'm leaving
her in good hands with you.

85
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,817
Don't worry, just be careful.

86
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,997
Listen, Tai, I want to come with you.

87
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,777
I won't get in the way, honest.

88
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:16,677
No way, you're my last line of defense.

89
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,457
What if the Dark Masters come, huh?

90
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,317
I need you here to look after the others.

91
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,576
You can count on me.

92
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,037
Don't worry, I'm on the job.

93
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,355
Yeah, leave it to us.

94
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,921
I knew I could count on you guys.

95
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:32,197
This place is deserted, but I still
get the feeling we're being followed.

96
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,398
Isn't that strange?

97
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:35,916
Izzy, what do you think you're doing?

98
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:36,870
Aha!

99
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,447
This is the digital age, Tai.

100
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:43,117
There are a lot simpler
ways of finding things now.

101
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,030
Good.

102
00:05:44,113 --> 00:05:46,112
I was beginning to get a crab in my wing.

103
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:49,080
I knew it.

104
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:50,897
There's an online map of the city.

105
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:52,217
Izzy, you're a genius.

106
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,130
Nice going.

107
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:56,320
Okay, now I'll search for
hospitals and pharmacies.

108
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,352
Jackpot, take your pick.

109
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,700
This one's the closest. Let's go.

110
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,720
Hey, wait for me.

111
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,134
I gotta unplug myself.

112
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,300
They have logged off.

113
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:11,260
Yes, my Lord Machinedramon, sir.

114
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:15,107
They've accessed maps and things
for hospitals and pharmacies.

115
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:16,210
Hi-o!

116
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,717
And you're waiting for what?

117
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,212
Show me those locations.

118
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:20,721
Right away, sir!

119
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:24,057
There are, uh, one, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven,

120
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:24,970
twelve of them!

121
00:06:25,053 --> 00:06:27,197
Let me put this in words
you can understand.

122
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,339
Send units to all twelve
locations and blow them up.

123
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,600
Oh, I get it now! Blow them up! Yes, sir!

124
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:36,600
Consider it already done, my lord.

125
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,856
A little fool has swallowed the bait.

126
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:43,040
Now it is time to spring the trap.

127
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:47,080
Uh-huh, uh-huh!

128
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:54,490
Finally!

129
00:06:54,573 --> 00:06:56,280
It was getting a little stuffy!

130
00:06:57,480 --> 00:07:01,009
No wonder this hospital is so
clean, there's no sick people.

131
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:03,050
Hello?

132
00:07:03,133 --> 00:07:03,963
Hello?

133
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:06,590
Tai!

134
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,515
Do you have any idea what you've done?

135
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:17,110
Tai?

136
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,280
Hey, over here!

137
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,675
I found the pharmacy!

138
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,817
There's a lot of medicine, all right.

139
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,717
How do we know what to
use for Kari's fever?

140
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:26,077
Strange as it sounds,
I wish Joe were here.

141
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,697
He might know what these are.

142
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,074
His father's a doctor.

143
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,877
That's a doctor's kid for you.

144
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,697
There's never one around
when you need him.

145
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:33,680
Huh? Hold on!

146
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,772
I can patch into the hospital's computer!

147
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,380
As he shoots, he scores!

148
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,580
Fever reduction. Children. Sir!

149
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:43,916
There they are, sir!

150
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:48,680
The network is being accessed
from inside Target 4, Master, sir.

151
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,317
Then wouldn't it be a good
idea to have all forces

152
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,106
converge on that target
and prepare to attack?

153
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,220
Oh, a brilliant idea, my lord, sir.

154
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:06,820
After you, Megadramon. Oh, no. After you.

155
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:11,197
Hey, Izzy, you sure
that's the right stuff?

156
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,097
It's the safest children's aspirin.

157
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,420
Good job, then let's get back. Fire!

158
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,480
Hey, let's beat it!

159
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:31,321
Lucky we're in a hospital, because
it looks like we might need one.

160
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:34,040
What are they? Nekanori-mon!

161
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,040
Evil robots with one job!

162
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,340
Blasting Digimon!

163
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,855
I suggest we get out of here and fast!

164
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,980
Target in range.

165
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:44,010
Green beam.

166
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:03,867
They brought along a friend.

167
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,960
Tankmon, an armor-plated bully
with a sneeze like a cannon.

168
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:09,877
If you think the other guys are bad,

169
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,784
these creeps have more
firepower than a volcano.

170
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:15,160
I thought we lost them.

171
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,977
How did they find us so quickly?

172
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:20,137
One of them must have been following
us and saw us come in here.

173
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:22,455
Big, Kari needs us to get back pronto.

174
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,920
Target in range.

175
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,020
Wind beam.

176
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,860
Hyper cannon!

177
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:33,670
Look out!

178
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:38,050
Duck!

179
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,010
Come on!

180
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:55,517
I'm really getting tired of that sound.

181
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,517
When are they gonna call
it quits and go home?

182
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,077
We don't have time for this.

183
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,077
I'm gonna go down there
and take care of them.

184
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,200
No, wait! Huh?

185
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,997
Those rolling arsenals
are just waiting for us.

186
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,917
We show ourselves and
they'll go ballistic.

187
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,337
So, we just hide here all day, is that it?

188
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,537
Those machines are the only
things moving out there,

189
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:14,517
so a map of the city's traffic
flow will show us where they are.

190
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,837
Then it's just a question of plotting
the best course to avoid them.

191
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,460
Yeah, just might work.

192
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,140
Of course it'll work.

193
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:22,640
You see?

194
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,937
There, I've pinpointed every one of them.

195
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:26,220
Good job, Izzy.

196
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,340
Excuse me, your metal myth.

197
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:32,837
They are accessing the network again,

198
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:35,940
but the access point is
relocated to sector B-17.

199
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:40,420
Then relay those coordinates
to all forces and attack.

200
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,260
Well, it's about time!

201
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:53,590
Inconceivable!

202
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:00,120
Incon-what? What now? The machines!

203
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:04,382
Every one of them rotated in sync
and now they're heading our way!

204
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,420
Of course!

205
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:09,197
They're zeroing in on
my computer connection!

206
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:10,700
Incoming! Huh?

207
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:12,450
Mom!

208
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:20,020
Digimon, digital monsters,
Digimon are the jump guns!

209
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:24,220
Digimon, digital monsters,
Digimon are the jump guns!

210
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,520
Pokémon, Digiball, toot!

211
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:33,280
Raymon!

212
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:35,650
Digimon!

213
00:11:35,733 --> 00:11:37,200
Aaaaaaah!

214
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:38,780
Nova Brown!

215
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:44,460
Get out of here!

216
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,110
Aaaaaah!

217
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:09,200
The plot sickens. Ah, me.

218
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:14,497
I had such high hopes that these little
ones would put on a more entertaining show.

219
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:19,020
But this, really, it's too tiresome.

220
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:24,469
Can we just get this over with and get
on to something a little less tedious?

221
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:27,400
There's no escape from Machine Drummond.

222
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:31,280
He's designed for total annihilation.

223
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,517
It's only a matter of time
now before he catches them.

224
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,400
And then the game is over.

225
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:40,257
Ah, it's not fair that that overgrown
can opener gets all the fun.

226
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:43,693
But I was so looking forward
to playing with them myself.

227
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,720
Farewell, little ones.

228
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:49,510
Digimon.

229
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,720
Digimon. Digimon.

230
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,170
Digital monsters.

231
00:12:54,253 --> 00:12:55,729
Digimon are the champions.

232
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,980
Digimon. Digital monsters.

233
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,809
Digimon are the champions.

234
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,237
Dream on Digimon.

235
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,420
Into...

236
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,060
Digimon!

237
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:07,960
Into ultimate!

238
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,740
Digimon! Digimon! Digimon!

239
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:15,280
Metal dream!

240
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,420
Digimon! Digimon!

241
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:30,017
Oh, I've got a teeny bit of bad news.

242
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,160
Nave escaped again, my lord, sir.

243
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:34,480
And yet you're still here.

244
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:38,440
It's all my fault.

245
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:43,617
I was giving away our location every
time I logged on with my computer.

246
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:45,777
How could I have not
thought of that before?

247
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:46,700
Good question.

248
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:48,115
Now we're stuck here.

249
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:51,791
Meanwhile, Kari's getting sicker
and sicker because of you.

250
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,580
Stop it, Tai.

251
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:56,095
What's come over you?

252
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:58,860
I'm sorry, Izzy.

253
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,612
Hey, Tai, this isn't your normal behavior.

254
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:04,950
It's Kari.

255
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,457
She almost died once before because of me.

256
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:08,370
Huh?

257
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:12,360
It happened when she was four
or five, just a little kid.

258
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:15,857
She stayed home from kindergarten
one day because she was sick.

259
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,037
I mean, I knew she was sick,

260
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:20,826
but all I could think about on
the way home was playing soccer.

261
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:21,980
Hey, I'm home.

262
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:26,957
I wanted to go out and play, but I
didn't want to leave her by herself.

263
